---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { socials } from '../config';

const interests = [
  'Empirical software engineering',
  'Game engine CI & build pipelines',
  'Automated crash triage & fault localization',
  'Identity architecture & ISO 27001',
  'Low-level graphics (Vulkan, OpenGL)',
  'Systems all the way down',
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who I am, what I build, and what keeps me curious.">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <div class="wayrule"></div>
  <h1 class="display h1">Hello.</h1>

  <p class="lede">I am Akil. I work across systems engineering, security, and developer tooling, with a strong drive toward empirical research in software engineering and game development systems.</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>By day, I lead IT systems and cybersecurity at Teams Squared, a global remote staffing firm placing skilled professionals from emerging markets into client teams worldwide. In practice, I am responsible for the architecture that controls who can touch what: identity governance on Microsoft Entra ID, endpoint security across distributed teams, and an organization-wide ISO 27001 ISMS. Working directly with client IT teams and heading our internal security function has given me a deep appreciation for systems that remain stable under real organizational pressure. It rewards asking the unglamorous questions: where are the hidden failure modes, and why does this workflow break?</p>

    <p>My foundation has always been software engineering. I graduated with a BSc in Computer Science from Dalhousie University (GPA 3.92, Sexton Scholar), where I focused on cybersecurity, web systems, and empirical methods. Alongside infrastructure, I continue to write the production software our team relies on daily, including an internal training LMS, a hardware fleet tracker, and modernizing our client portal. Having built applications from the database schema up to the authentication layer is what makes security and systems stability intuitive to me: I know where software tends to leak because I have built it myself.</p>

    <p>Before my current role, I spent a co-op term as a Gameplay Programmer at Ubisoft Halifax, building Unity and C# systems for unannounced titles: dynamic Cinemachine camera-clipping, NavMesh targeting over hex grids, and AI behavior trees. Games and interactive graphics remain my core technical passion. I build custom renderers from scratch in Vulkan and OpenGL to understand how memory buffers, pipelines, and shaders transform geometry into pixels, and I regularly prototype gameplay mechanics in Godot.</p>

    <p>Living between production game development and enterprise infrastructure exposed a persistent frustration: academic developer tooling and automated program repair techniques are almost exclusively benchmarked on small, single-threaded Java suites like Defects4J. They rarely account for the realities of modern game engines: multi-gigabyte binary asset baking, link-time optimization bottlenecks, physics loop non-determinism, and cross-language crashes. This gap is what motivates my research ambition. I want to conduct rigorous empirical software engineering research that tackles continuous integration build friction, automated crash triage, and fault localization where it actually hurts developer workflows.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sec-label" id="looking">What I'm looking for</h2>
  <p class="seeking">I am actively exploring opportunities in empirical software engineering research (including graduate research labs and applied industrial R&amp;D groups), as well as systems engineering, developer infrastructure, and security roles. I hold a Canadian post-graduation work permit (PGWP) valid through June 2029 and am open to relocating anywhere in Canada, including through the Atlantic Immigration Program. If you are investigating developer tooling, engine reliability, or complex systems, I would welcome a conversation.</p>

  <h2 class="sec-label">What keeps me curious</h2>
  <ul class="interests">
    {interests.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="sec-label">Elsewhere</h2>
  <ul class="contact">
    {socials.map((s) => (
      <li>
        <span class="c-label">{s.label}</span>
        <a href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.handle ?? s.label}</a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.4rem); margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--ink-muted); line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 58ch; margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink); }
  .seeking {
    max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.6;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--cobalt); padding-left: var(--space-2);
  }
  .sec-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-2);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
  .interests { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .interests li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-muted);
    background: var(--paper-panel); padding: 5px 11px;
  }
  .contact { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: var(--space-2); max-width: 32rem; }
  .contact li {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr; gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-1) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8125rem; align-items: baseline;
  }
  .contact li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .c-label { color: var(--ink-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.6875rem; }
  .contact a { color: var(--cobalt); text-decoration: none; word-break: break-word; }
  .contact a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .contact li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; }
  }
</style>
